All redistributed copies of the Software, whether modified or unmodified, must include this license text in full.

2.3 Functional Accessibility Requirement

The Software, when distributed or deployed, must not include mechanisms that restrict core functionality based on payment, subscription status, or access tier.

For clarity, the following are prohibited in any distribution of the Software:
- paywalls or forced subscriptions
- disabling functionality after a trial period
- restricting core functionality to paid tiers


All functionality included in the Software must be accessible without payment.

This clause does not prohibit:
- optional paid hosting or infrastructure services external to the Software
- optional paid support or consulting services
- voluntary donations or sponsorship

2.4 Optional Payment Solicitation

The Software may display optional and non-blocking messages requesting voluntary payment, donation, or sponsorship.

Such messages must:
- not prevent or interrupt normal use of the Software
- not be presented as mandatory

